    "Full API spec": "Repository structure and import graph (acyclic): errors.py -> types.py -> template.py -> validation.py -> press_release.py -> search.py -> __init__.py -> Main.py -> tests/test_main.py. No module may import datetime, time, random, uuid, pathlib, os, threading, or any clock abstraction.\n\npress_releases/errors.py:\n- class DomainError(ValueError): domain-level error for invalid entity state or operation. No additional members.\n- class InvalidTransitionError(DomainError): raised for invalid lifecycle transitions. No additional members.\n\npress_releases/types.py:\n- enum State(Enum): DRAFT, REVIEW, PUBLISHED. Represents lifecycle states of a press release.\n- @dataclass(frozen=True) class Contact: fields name: str, email: str. Value object; uses only generated __init__.\n- @dataclass(frozen=True) class VersionEntry: fields number: int, rendered_text: str. Value object; uses only generated __init__.\n\npress_releases/template.py:\n- @dataclass(frozen=True) class Template:\n  - name: str\n  - content: str\n  - def render(self, fields: dict[str, str] | None = None) -> str: Deterministic literal substitution that leaves unknown placeholders intact. Implementation is exactly:\n    values = {} if fields is None else fields\n    result = self.content\n    for key in sorted(values):\n        result = result.replace(\"{{\" + key + \"}}\", values[key])\n    return result\n  Forbidden: parsing via split/regex/open-ended scanning; only the exact sorted key replacement loop is used.\n\npress_releases/validation.py:\n- def validate_headline(headline: str) -> bool: Returns True if headline is non-blank (after stripping), else False. Never raises.\n- def validate_body(body: str) -> bool: Returns True if body is non-blank (after stripping), else False. Never raises.\n- def validate_contact(contact: Contact) -> bool: Returns True if contact.name is non-blank (after stripping) and contact.email contains exactly one '@' with non-empty local part and domain part; otherwise False. Never raises.\n\npress_releases/press_release.py:\n- class PressRelease:\n  - Constructor: def __init__(self, id: str, headline: str, body: str, contact: Contact, template: Template, custom_fields: dict[str, str] | None = None) -> None\n    Behavior: ordinary mutable class (no @dataclass). Assigns internal attributes (_id, _headline, _body, _contact, _template, _custom_fields dict copy if provided else empty dict, _state starts State.DRAFT, _tags_list empty list, _tags_set empty set, _versions empty list). The constructor does not validate and never throws for invalid values so tests can construct invalid candidates.\n  - Properties (read-only): id: str, headline: str, body: str, contact: Contact, state: State. Expose underlying fields without side effects.\n  - def validate(self) -> bool: Orchestrates validations using validate_headline, validate_body, validate_contact; returns False on any invalid part; never raises.\n  - def submit_for_review(self) -> None: If validate() is False, raise DomainError. Otherwise, requires current state is State.DRAFT; if not, raise InvalidTransitionError. On success sets state to State.REVIEW.\n  - def publish(self) -> None: Requires current state is State.REVIEW; otherwise raise InvalidTransitionError. On first successful publish, set state to State.PUBLISHED and append exactly VersionEntry(number=1, rendered_text=self.render_plain_text()). Further publish attempts from non-REVIEW states should raise InvalidTransitionError; no additional version entries are added beyond the first publish as per requirement.\n  - def add_tag(self, tag: str) -> None: Trim tag via tag.strip(). If empty after trim, raise DomainError. If not already present (based on exact string match, case-sensitive), add to _tags_list and _tags_set preserving insertion order.\n  - def tags(self) -> list[str]: Returns a defensive copy (new list) of tags in insertion order.\n  - def render_plain_text(self) -> str: Build a fields dict combining custom_fields with canonical keys: 'headline' -> self._headline, 'body' -> self._body, 'contact' -> self._contact.name, 'contact_name' -> self._contact.name, 'contact_email' -> self._contact.email. Call self._template.render(fields) and return the result.\n  - def version_history(self) -> list[VersionEntry]: Returns a defensive copy (new list) of the version entries.\n  Errors: Uses DomainError for invalid content submission; InvalidTransitionError for invalid state transitions.\n\npress_releases/search.py:\n- def search_by_tag(releases: list[PressRelease], tag: str) -> list[PressRelease]: Returns a new list preserving the order of non-None input entries whose tags include an exact normalized tag match. Normalization is trim-only (tag.strip()). Matching is exact string equality (case-sensitive) against stored tags. Never mutates inputs.\n- def search_text(releases: list[PressRelease], query: str) -> list[PressRelease]: Returns a new list preserving order of non-None releases whose headline or body contains the query case-insensitively (both sides lowered). Never mutates inputs.\n\npress_releases/__init__.py:\n- Re-exports only the canonical names from submodules: DomainError, InvalidTransitionError; State, Contact, VersionEntry; Template; validate_headline, validate_body, validate_contact; PressRelease; search_by_tag, search_text. MUST NOT export or mention run_demo.\n\nMain.py:\n- def run_demo() -> dict[str, object]: Using absolute imports from press_releases, constructs a Template, Contact, and PressRelease, validates, adds a tag (e.g., 'media'), transitions DRAFT -> REVIEW -> PUBLISHED, triggers rendering and versioning, then returns a dict with representative keys such as {'release': PressRelease, 'state': State.PUBLISHED, 'rendered': str, 'versions': list[VersionEntry] or 'version_count': int}. Under if __name__ == '__main__': prints at most one concise line (e.g., the final state or rendered headline) and exits.\n\ntests/test_main.py:\n- Must contain exactly three tests as specified:\n  1) Demo test: from Main import run_demo (separate literal line). Assert returned value is dict and state is State.PUBLISHED.\n  2) Rendering/validation/lifecycle/version test: Template('basic','{{headline}}|{{body}}|{{contact_email}}'), Contact('Alice','a@b.com'), PressRelease(..., headline='Hello', body='Body', ...). validate() True; submit_for_review(); publish(); version_history() length exactly 1; entry.number == 1; entry.rendered_text == 'Hello|Body|a@b.com'.\n  3) Invalid/transition/tags/search test: Construct invalid candidate with blank headline and Contact('','invalid'); candidate.validate() is False; with pytest.raises(DomainError): candidate.submit_for_review(). Construct separate valid_draft with headline 'Hello' and body; without calling submit_for_review(), assert with pytest.raises(InvalidTransitionError): valid_draft.publish(). Then add 'media' then 'news' tags; tags() order preserved; search_by_tag([valid_draft], ' media ') returns [valid_draft]; search_text([valid_draft], 'hello') returns [valid_draft]. The third test MUST NOT call valid_draft.submit_for_review() before its expected failing publish.\n\nNon-negotiable constraints reiterated:\n- Exact file list (10 files): requirements.txt; press_releases/errors.py; press_releases/types.py; press_releases/template.py; press_releases/validation.py; press_releases/press_release.py; press_releases/search.py; press_releases/__init__.py; Main.py; tests/test_main.py.\n- Ordinary mutable PressRelease (no dataclass); only Contact, VersionEntry, Template are frozen dataclasses with generated initializers.\n- Template.render uses exactly the literal sorted-keys replacement loop described; no split/slice/regex parsing.\n- Constructor of PressRelease never validates; validate() returns False on invalid; submit_for_review raises DomainError on invalid content; invalid publish from DRAFT raises InvalidTransitionError.\n- Version history uses integer numbers; on first publish append exactly VersionEntry(1, rendered_plain_text()).\n- __init__.py re-exports only canonical API; never mentions run_demo.\n- tests/test_main.py must include a separate literal line `from Main import run_demo` and must not import run_demo from press_releases.\n- Main.py prints at most one concise line under the __name__ guard.\n- No imports of datetime/time/random/uuid/pathlib/os/threading anywhere.\n",
    "Shared Knowledge": "We implement a medium-size Python 3.10 repository for Custom press releases. Core domain logic resides under the press_releases package with an acyclic import graph: errors -> types -> template -> validation -> press_release -> search -> __init__.py. Main.py is the environment-dependent entrypoint providing run_demo() and a single guarded print. tests/test_main.py is the only protocol-level test file; it imports run_demo from Main on its own line and imports all domain symbols from press_releases. The domain covers templates with sorted-keys literal replacement, validation returning booleans, a DRAFT->REVIEW->PUBLISHED lifecycle with domain exceptions, deterministic version history with integer numbering, tags with trim uniqueness and insertion order, and search utilities that preserve input order and never mutate inputs.",
    "Execution Protocol": "Test command: python -m pytest -q. Runtime entry: Main.py defines run_demo(), uses absolute press_releases imports, and prints at most one concise line under the __name__ guard. Single protocol-level test target: tests/test_main.py with exactly three tests covering demo to PUBLISHED, rendering/validation/lifecycle/versioning, and invalid flow plus tags/search. Tests are deterministic, headless, offline, and interact only with the canonical public API.",
    "Anything UNCLEAR": ""
}
